  "id": "COMPOUND:43279 - PROTEIN:5780",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3alpha)- and SQ20B, mediated through multiple targets. The core mechanism appears to involve the interaction of Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3alpha)- with the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is a known target of several compounds, including 5-Oxobrucine and Methyl valerate. These compounds, in turn, are targets of SQ20B, indicating a chain of molecular interactions where Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3alpha)- acts as a precursor or modulator of the downstream targets. The scores from the paths suggest a strong, though not absolute, correlation, likely due to the overlapping biological roles of these compounds in regulating proteasome activity. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3alpha)- to influence SQ20B through a series of intermediate targets, emphasizing its role in modulating proteasome function and potentially affecting cellular processes.",
